{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "26", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "28", "S": "06"}}, "news": [{"title": "Bihar CM forms panel to look into notices over commercial activities in residential buildings", "para": "Bihar Chief Minister Samrat Choudhary has taken a decisive step by forming a committee aimed at scrutinizing the Patna Municipal Corporation's recent notices. Chaired by Deputy Chief Minister Vijay Kumar Choudhary, this committee is set to delve into the implications of commercial ventures within residential areas and will deliver recommendations that prioritize community welfare, especially following the legislators\u2019 urgent memorandum addressing these concerns.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/commercial/bihar-cm-forms-panel-to-look-into-notices-over-commercial-activities-in-residential-buildings/133531022?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-80880/133531022.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "commercial"}, {"title": "About 3.5 lakh new PMAY homes approved for Assam: Chief minister", "para": "Assam Chief Minister Himanta Biswa Sarma engaged with Union Agriculture Minister Shivraj Singh Chouhan, securing approval for the construction of 3.1 lakh homes under the PM Awas Yojana. This initiative marks an investment of Rs 5,000 crore aimed at enhancing housing in Assam, particularly benefiting areas affected by flooding. Furthermore, the state has been granted Rs 139 crore dedicated to agricultural development projects.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/about-3-5-lakh-new-pmay-homes-approved-for-assam-chief-minister/133530915?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-124958/133530915.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Cyberabad civic body orders crackdown on illegal buildings built on 75 sq yards, demolishes nine structures", "para": "Following a serious incident involving a building collapse, the Cyberabad Municipal Corporation is enhancing its crackdown on illegal constructions. A total of 38 structures have been flagged for enforcement actions. The focus is on those taller than permitted limits on compact plots, while also addressing projects on larger plots that lack the necessary permits. Continuous daily inspections are in place to ensure adherence to building regulations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/cyberabad-civic-body-orders-crackdown-on-illegal-buildings-built-on-75-sq-yards-demolishes-nine-structures/133529922?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-261350/133529922.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}